        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "<p>Prove \\(\\underset{x→-\\infty}{lim}\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}=0\\).</p>\n<p>\\(|\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}-0|&lt;\\varepsilon Definition ofalimit|\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}|&lt;\\varepsilonSubtract.\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}&lt;\\varepsilon(x-3)^{2}&gt;0\\frac{8}{\\varepsilon}&lt;(x-3)^{2}Rewrite.\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\varepsilon}}&lt;|x-3|Takethesquareroot.-\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\varepsilon}}&gt;x-3 Positive squarerootbecausexapproachesnegativeinfinity-\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\varepsilon}}+3&gt;xAdd.\\)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>So if \\(N=\\) \\(-\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{\\varepsilon}}+3\\), then \\(\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\) is within \\(\\varepsilon\\) of 0.</p>"
